Here's the full testsmells.org 19-smell academic audit of your integration test suite.

---

## Summary Dashboard

| Severity | Smell Count | Affected Tests |
|----------|-------------|----------------|
| High     | 3           | 3              |
| Medium   | 1           | 1              |
| Low      | 0           | 0              |
| **Total**| **4**       | **4 of 8**     |

**Framework:** MSTest 4.1.0 · .NET 10 · Class marked `[TestCategory("Integration")]`

---

## Findings by Severity

### 🔴 HIGH — Sleepy Test

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `NotifyOnInsert_SendsEventAfterDelay` (line 87)

```csharp
Thread.Sleep(3000);   // blocks for 3 seconds — non-deterministic
```

Even in integration tests, `Thread.Sleep` is a smell. If the notification system is slow, 3 s may not be enough; if it's fast, you waste 3 s per run.

**Fix — poll with a timeout:**
```csharp
var cts = new CancellationTokenSource(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(5));
while (!_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id))
{
    await Task.Delay(50, cts.Token);
}
Assert.IsTrue(_repository.WasNotificationSent(user.Id));
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Flaky failures in CI; inflated suite runtime.

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Conditional Test Logic

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` (lines 101–108)

```csharp
if (loaded is PremiumUser premium)
{
    Assert.IsTrue(premium.DiscountRate > 0);
}
else
{
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded!.Name);
}
```

The `if/else` means **one branch never executes** — the test silently skips half its logic. If `loaded` is never a `PremiumUser`, the discount-rate assertion is dead code; if it always is, the name assertion is dead code.

**Fix — split into two explicit tests:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_StandardUser_ReturnsCorrectName()
{
    _repository.Insert(new User("eve@example.com", "Eve"));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("eve@example.com");
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.AreEqual("Eve", loaded.Name);
}

[TestMethod]
public void GetUser_PremiumUser_HasPositiveDiscount()
{
    _repository.Insert(new PremiumUser("vip@example.com", "VIP", discountRate: 0.1m));
    var loaded = _repository.GetByEmail("vip@example.com") as PremiumUser;
    Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
    Assert.IsTrue(loaded.DiscountRate > 0);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Hidden gap — you think both paths are tested, but only one ever runs.

---

### 🔴 HIGH — Assertion-Free Test (Unknown Test)

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors` (lines 113–119)

```csharp
public void BulkInsert_RunsWithoutErrors()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }
}
```

No assertion at all. MSTest reports this as "passed" even if every insert silently corrupts data. The name implies "no errors," but the framework guarantees a pass as long as no exception is thrown — that's a very low bar.

**Fix — assert the outcome:**
```csharp
[TestMethod]
public void BulkInsert_PersistsAllRecords()
{
    for (int i = 0; i < 100; i++)
    {
        _repository.Insert(new User($"bulk{i}@example.com", $"Bulk User {i}"));
    }

    var users = _repository.ListAll();
    Assert.AreEqual(100, users.Count);
}
```

**Risk if unfixed:** False confidence — 100 % pass rate with 0 % verification.

---

### 🟡 MEDIUM — Assertion Roulette

**File:** `UserRepositoryIntegrationTests.cs` · **Method:** `InsertUser_PersistsToDatabase` (lines 35–38)

```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded);
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name);
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email);
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0);
```

Four assertions with no message parameters. When one fails in CI, the failure log says `Assert.AreEqual failed. Expected:<Alice>. Actual:<null>` without context on *which property* was wrong.

**Fix — add message parameters:**
```csharp
Assert.IsNotNull(loaded, "Loaded user should not be null after insert");
Assert.AreEqual("Alice", loaded.Name, "Name should match inserted value");
Assert.AreEqual("alice@example.com", loaded.Email, "Email should match inserted value");
Assert.IsTrue(loaded.Id > 0, "Auto-generated Id should be positive");
```

**Risk if unfixed:** Slower diagnosis during CI failures — developers must open the source to find which assertion failed and why.

---

## Smell-Free Patterns ✅

**4 of 8 tests are clean** and follow good practices:

| Method | Good Pattern |
|--------|-------------|
| `UpdateUser_ModifiesExistingRecord` | Clear arrange-act-assert, focused scope |
| `DeleteUser_RemovesFromDatabase` | Clean null-check assertion for absence |
| `ListUsers_ReturnsAllInserted` | Count assertion (3) is contextually obvious (3 items just added) — **not** Magic Number |
| `InsertUser_ConcurrentInserts_MaintainsIntegrity` | Proper async/await, clean assertion on count |

**Integration-test calibration applied:** The in-memory SQLite setup is hermetic (not a Mystery Guest); no test calls 4+ distinct production methods (no Eager Test). These are well-scoped integration tests.

---

## Prioritized Remediation Plan

| Priority | Smell | Fix | Effort |
|----------|-------|-----|--------|
| 1 | **Assertion-Free Test** | Add `Assert.AreEqual(100, ...)` to `BulkInsert` | ~2 min |
| 2 | **Conditional Test Logic** | Split `GetUser_ReturnsCorrectType` into 2 tests | ~5 min |
| 3 | **Sleepy Test** | Replace `Thread.Sleep(3000)` with polling loop | ~10 min |
| 4 | **Assertion Roulette** | Add message strings to 4 assertions in `InsertUser` | ~2 min |

Priorities 1–2 address **silent false-passes** (tests that pass but verify nothing or skip branches). Priority 3 reduces **flakiness and runtime**. Priority 4 is a **diagnostic improvement** with low urgency.
